WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.883 --> 00:00:06.980
(clearing throat)

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.790
- You go back to the intersection,

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:12.050
you make a left at the
dead tree, you're welcome.

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.120
- What? No. I'm not lost.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.220
- Trust me you are.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:18.270
- Ha ha, funny, say, nice boat,

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.570
any chance you might
actually get on it today?

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:23.760
- What was that?

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.210
- New postman, Smeerensburg,
which is on an island,

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.530
which is surrounded by water,

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:30.920
which I need a boat to
get to, which you have.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.923
Are we starting to connect the dots?

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:35.003
- Hmm-mm.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.780
- Is the weather always like this?

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.993
- Eh, we having a bit of a heatwave.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.220
- Where is everyone?

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.400
- Everyone?

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.000
- I thought there would be
some sort of a reception.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:54.500
- Oh. Right, right the reception,
of course the reception.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.510
It's good you reminded me.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:57.320
You just ring the bell over there,

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.820
and then then reception will start.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:00.840
- The bell?

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.210
- Yep. Give it a go, and they'll come out.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.297
Why they'll have a band, hors d'oeuvres

00:01:05.297 --> 00:01:10.160
and a, and a key to the city,
all that reception stuff.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.270
- Really? Out here.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:13.550
- Why of course.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:17.040
Well it's not everyday they
get a brand new postman

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.133
from the big city.

00:01:20.935 --> 00:01:24.188
(bell ringing)

00:01:24.188 --> 00:01:25.480
(dramatic orchestral music)

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.647
(yelling)

00:01:36.795 --> 00:01:38.462
- What's happening?!

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.940
- Alright, I'm gonna just
take wild guess here.

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:47.410
You are the latest mailman

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:50.341
and the ferryman tricked you
into ringing the battle-bell.

00:01:50.341 --> 00:01:51.550
- Ah there you are!

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:54.833
I'd wondered where you'd
scurried off to, come on sport!

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:58.160
- What happened here?

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.970
- Oh. Um. Colorful local traditions.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.740
Quirky folklore, that kinda thing.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:06.300
All part of this quaint
town's vibrant culture.

00:02:17.636 --> 00:02:20.553
(orchestral music)

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.197
- Home, sweet home.

00:02:24.197 --> 00:02:27.197
(chickens clucking)

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:32.680
- Well, lots of nice, natural light,

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:35.610
rustic touches, central
air and panoramic views,

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:37.223
perfect for animal lovers.

00:02:38.587 --> 00:02:39.460
Enjoy.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:40.373
- Wait, wait.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:43.970
Okay, get low, don't panic, don't panic.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.541
- Ah, I guess that's why
they call it snail mail.

00:02:46.541 --> 00:02:47.374
(dogs barking)

00:02:47.374 --> 00:02:49.860
- Ah. Good puppies, good puppies. Ah, ah.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.083
- And that must be the express mail.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:56.536
- Is this is a bad time, I
can see you're pretty swamped.

00:02:56.536 --> 00:02:57.960
(sigh)

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.692
Don't you have a job or something?

00:03:00.692 --> 00:03:03.450
Don't you have a job or something?

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.840
- Why sure I do.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.930
I'm here to pick up all the outgoing mail.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:09.300
So, where is it?

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.530
Now you're gonna have to help
me with the heavier bags.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.000
Bad back don't you know?

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.550
- Man, I hate you.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:15.383
- I know.

00:03:15.383 --> 00:03:17.940
So eh, where, where is the mail anyway?

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:20.680
What do you keep it in a
different room now or something?

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:22.950
What about if I walk around the room,

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:26.950
if I get close to the
mail, you say warmer.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:31.950
And if I'm getting further
from the mail, you say colder.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:32.993
And then...

00:03:32.993 --> 00:03:33.826
- What's that?

00:03:33.826 --> 00:03:35.860
- What? Oh, the Woodsman's cabin?

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.550
- Yeah. Does someone live there?

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.480
- Oh sure. Yeah you
should definitely drop by,

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.710
nice fella, loves visitors.

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:46.630
- Jesper Johansson, postman.
We've never properly...

00:03:49.053 --> 00:03:51.209
Oh uh.

00:03:51.209 --> 00:03:53.470
- Ah. Young love.

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:54.960
Takes me back you know.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.270
The intense looks, the
palpitation of the heart.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.800
The whimpering, the
soiling of the pants, no.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.100
I can't relate to so much of.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.017
(sigh)

00:04:05.072 --> 00:04:06.739
mwaa mwaa mwaa mwaa!

